WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.191 --> 00:00:03.277
(elegant orchestral music)

00:00:03.277 --> 00:00:04.601
- I didn't bring you here
just to sip some tea,

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:05.880
I wanted to spill some tea.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.232
So, I thought of a game.

00:00:07.232 --> 00:00:08.738
I like to call it "Sip It and Spill It"

00:00:08.738 --> 00:00:10.401
and it's basically a very sophisticated

00:00:10.401 --> 00:00:12.019
version of Never Have I Ever.

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:12.852
So, I'll start.

00:00:12.852 --> 00:00:14.873
Because there's something I'm
actually very interested in,

00:00:14.873 --> 00:00:18.129
and I've never seen a ghost,
and I wanna see a ghost,

00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:19.289
and I'm very mad that I haven't.

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:22.669
Have you ever been scared by
the Highclere Castle ghost?

00:00:22.669 --> 00:00:24.694
(rock guitar)

00:00:24.694 --> 00:00:25.882
Okay, you're sipping.

00:00:25.882 --> 00:00:26.894
- I haven't been scared by it,

00:00:26.894 --> 00:00:28.662
but put it this way:
when Shirley MacClaine

00:00:28.662 --> 00:00:31.374
was on the show,
Oh, of course, Shirley...

00:00:31.374 --> 00:00:32.207
she of course has probably lived at

00:00:32.207 --> 00:00:33.772
Highclere Castle in the past.

00:00:33.772 --> 00:00:35.306
(group laughing)

00:00:35.306 --> 00:00:37.139
And she said he's been
in this room before.

00:00:37.139 --> 00:00:38.590
He's been sat there having dinner.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.597
So I think that's one step
removed from being in touch...

00:00:40.597 --> 00:00:41.719
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:41.719 --> 00:00:42.780
- She was there the day
before we were filming though,

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:43.613
wasn't she?

00:00:43.613 --> 00:00:44.446
- Yeah!

00:00:44.446 --> 00:00:45.827
- This is why I love her,
she's slightly nutty.

00:00:45.827 --> 00:00:47.365
We have the same birthday,
I'm slightly nutty.

00:00:47.365 --> 00:00:49.931
So yeah, Tauruses are all weird.

00:00:49.931 --> 00:00:52.826
But yes, but we're fun, right?

00:00:52.826 --> 00:00:54.577
All right, so anybody wanna go now?

00:00:54.577 --> 00:00:56.415
Maybe Elizabeth, you wanna go?

00:00:56.415 --> 00:00:59.481
- Sip it and spill it if you have

00:00:59.481 --> 00:01:02.381
a DJ alter-ego at this table.

00:01:02.381 --> 00:01:03.798
- A DJ alter-ego.

00:01:05.122 --> 00:01:05.955
What!?

00:01:06.821 --> 00:01:08.346
What, what?

00:01:08.346 --> 00:01:09.212
- Okay, so.

00:01:09.212 --> 00:01:10.391
- Tell us more!

00:01:10.391 --> 00:01:13.025
- I'm always that person at a party.

00:01:13.025 --> 00:01:14.449
I get all the tunes going and everything,

00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:16.940
and my Spotify playlist
is called DJ Doggard's.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:19.346
However, that has recently been blown

00:01:19.346 --> 00:01:20.560
out of proportion--
Escalated a bit.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.591
- And apparently I'm spinning
the decks in Ibiza every year,

00:01:23.591 --> 00:01:24.774
which is not true.

00:01:24.774 --> 00:01:26.053
(group laughing)

00:01:26.053 --> 00:01:27.350
- Okay Michelle, go ahead.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.659
- Sip it and spill it if you're
related to Indiana Jones.

00:01:30.659 --> 00:01:32.590
- Harrison Ford?

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:33.423
(chimes twinkling)

00:01:33.423 --> 00:01:34.577
- What!?

00:01:34.577 --> 00:01:35.410
- Ooh!

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:38.143
- My grandfather was an explorer,

00:01:38.143 --> 00:01:41.474
and he was the first white
man to go into Tibet,

00:01:41.474 --> 00:01:44.030
and he wrote a book
about it, and then he did

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:46.809
a whole bunch of exploring in his life,

00:01:46.809 --> 00:01:49.913
and somebody on Google made up that he was

00:01:49.913 --> 00:01:52.395
the inspiration for Indiana Jones.

00:01:52.395 --> 00:01:54.170
- [Hugh] Oh, the real Indiana Jones.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.003
- Yeah.

00:01:55.003 --> 00:01:56.788
- That's way cooler than
the Harrison Ford thing.

00:01:56.788 --> 00:01:57.929
I thought that was what happened.

00:01:57.929 --> 00:01:58.910
I was like, "Oh, okay."

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.182
Cool, okay.
Harrison Ford!

00:02:00.182 --> 00:02:02.205
- He's pretty cool.

00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:03.091
- I still like you, Harrison.

00:02:03.091 --> 00:02:03.924
- All right.

00:02:03.924 --> 00:02:05.844
(group laughing)

00:02:05.844 --> 00:02:07.798
- Sip it or spill it if you've ever

00:02:07.798 --> 00:02:10.050
ridden a bicycle on a motorway.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:11.617
(suspenseful drums)

00:02:11.617 --> 00:02:13.554
(twinkling chimes)

00:02:13.554 --> 00:02:14.387
- What?

00:02:14.387 --> 00:02:16.787
I wanna be friends with you.

00:02:16.787 --> 00:02:19.324
- I decided to shake it up a little,

00:02:19.324 --> 00:02:23.080
and instead of taking the
car to the dance rehearsal,

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.961
I would ride my bike
to the dance rehearsal.

00:02:24.961 --> 00:02:26.776
And everything was going
well, and I had my helmet on,

00:02:26.776 --> 00:02:29.292
and I was going, and I went
up this little slip road,

00:02:29.292 --> 00:02:30.125
suddenly they were like

00:02:30.125 --> 00:02:31.176
(cars whooshing)

00:02:31.176 --> 00:02:32.666
and I was riding
Oh my God.

00:02:32.666 --> 00:02:33.527
- I was on a freeway.

00:02:33.527 --> 00:02:34.360
- [Kelly] Whoa.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.264
- I had taken a wrong turn.

00:02:35.264 --> 00:02:36.442
- [Kelly] And you were
going the opposite way?

00:02:36.442 --> 00:02:37.275
- And I was like, "F--"

00:02:37.275 --> 00:02:38.411
(car horns beeping)

00:02:38.411 --> 00:02:39.970
(group laughing)

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:40.803
- [Kelly] And you weren't--

00:02:40.803 --> 00:02:43.675
- Like this, and everyone
was honking at me.

00:02:43.675 --> 00:02:46.840
It was like, terrible, dream.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.231
And I was just trying to
get to my dance rehearsal.

00:02:49.231 --> 00:02:51.480
I was like, "I'm just going
to the dance rehearsal!"

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:56.480
And then, I finally, I finally
got off the next off-ramp,

00:02:56.589 --> 00:03:00.213
made it to the, I came into the rehearsal.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:05.054
I was-- sweat, literally
pouring down my face, sweat.

00:03:05.054 --> 00:03:06.215
(grunting)

00:03:06.215 --> 00:03:07.387
These two.

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:08.416
- We just look at the door,

00:03:08.416 --> 00:03:09.828
she was there, like--
You would never let

00:03:09.828 --> 00:03:11.444
me forget it.

00:03:11.444 --> 00:03:12.277
- "Never again."

00:03:12.277 --> 00:03:13.554
(men laughing)

00:03:13.554 --> 00:03:14.865
- I mean, look at him.

00:03:14.865 --> 00:03:15.963
- Wait, you're hilarious.

00:03:15.963 --> 00:03:18.612
Were you going the opposite way
then, of all the other cars?

00:03:18.612 --> 00:03:20.134
- Ah, I don't remember which way I was--

00:03:20.134 --> 00:03:21.953
- She was heading for Heathrow.

00:03:21.953 --> 00:03:22.918
- Okay, it was like--

00:03:22.918 --> 00:03:25.969
- I don't have a great sense of direction.

00:03:25.969 --> 00:03:26.802
- I don't either.

00:03:26.802 --> 00:03:27.918
- Really!?

00:03:27.918 --> 00:03:28.970
- I don't.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:30.058
You have no sense of direction.

00:03:30.058 --> 00:03:31.146
- There's nothing you can do about it.

00:03:31.146 --> 00:03:32.108
- I'm you.

00:03:32.108 --> 00:03:34.423
I would've been the one lost
for three hours in the dark.

00:03:34.423 --> 00:03:35.915
- Do you know, I went for a walk--

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.134
- [Michelle] She went for a walk!

00:03:37.134 --> 00:03:38.647
- I went for a little
walk on Highclere Castle.

00:03:38.647 --> 00:03:40.517
- She went, "I'm just gonna go for a walk"

00:03:40.517 --> 00:03:41.976
during the lunch break.

00:03:41.976 --> 00:03:43.652
And then it was getting closer and closer

00:03:43.652 --> 00:03:45.417
to the time we needed to go on set.

00:03:45.417 --> 00:03:46.723
- We couldn't--

00:03:46.723 --> 00:03:47.914
- You went on a hike!

00:03:47.914 --> 00:03:49.052
- We couldn't find her.

00:03:49.052 --> 00:03:51.320
- I'm you, I get lost very easily.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.587
I don't know if I've ever gotten on a road

00:03:53.587 --> 00:03:54.991
with a bicycle.
Can you imagine

00:03:54.991 --> 00:03:56.792
some of the people on that road?

00:03:56.792 --> 00:03:58.261
- What they must have thought.

00:03:58.261 --> 00:03:59.544
- Especially if they notice you.

00:03:59.544 --> 00:04:01.169
- Suddenly they're like, "Is that lady--"

00:04:01.169 --> 00:04:02.669
- "Do I know her?"

00:04:03.826 --> 00:04:05.726
- That's the best part!

00:04:05.726 --> 00:04:07.426
Okay, okay okay.

00:04:07.426 --> 00:04:08.601
I do want to talk about though,

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:10.525
let's talk about the movie, though.

00:04:10.525 --> 00:04:12.085
Everybody's so excited about it.

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:13.898
- This really deserves to
be seen on a big screen

00:04:13.898 --> 00:04:17.372
because it's so much more
sort of lush and vibrant

00:04:17.372 --> 00:04:19.626
and epic than we had even on the TV show,

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:21.231
which in itself was quite cinematic.

00:04:21.231 --> 00:04:22.937
And I think that's the major difference.

00:04:22.937 --> 00:04:24.405
I think fans who've followed the show

00:04:24.405 --> 00:04:25.955
from the beginning will be delighted

00:04:25.955 --> 00:04:27.791
that it's a continuation of the story,

00:04:27.791 --> 00:04:28.624
and even for people who don't know

00:04:28.624 --> 00:04:32.883
the characters and the series,
it's a stand-alone story.

00:04:32.883 --> 00:04:35.933
And it was really the support
of the fans that drove it,

00:04:35.933 --> 00:04:37.487
that got us all back together, because

00:04:37.487 --> 00:04:39.011
I think if that appetite hadn't been there

00:04:39.011 --> 00:04:41.230
from the fans, then we
wouldn't be sitting here now

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:42.281
at your lovely tea table.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:43.641
- All right, sip it and spill it

00:04:43.641 --> 00:04:46.276
if you've had the
greatest time ever at the

00:04:46.276 --> 00:04:47.109
most amazing--
Yay! Cheers to that!

00:04:47.109 --> 00:04:47.942
- Oh!

00:04:47.942 --> 00:04:49.299
- We never do that!

00:04:49.299 --> 00:04:51.045
Well, you do in America, Hugh.

00:04:51.045 --> 00:04:52.515
- Oh, just sip it and stop it, Hugh.

00:04:52.515 --> 00:04:55.215
(Kelly laughing)
(orchestral finale)

